SUMMARY:A Dream Within A Dream: The Poetry and Stories of Edgar Allan Poe
DESCRIPTION:A Dream Within A Dream: The Poetry and Stories of Edgar Allan Poe\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				TuesdayOctober 27\, 202610:00am \n  \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Runtime: 90 minutes\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Age Recommendation:\nGrades 8 – 12\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Advisory: This production uses haze. \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n\n\n Share: \n \n\n\n\n\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Pricing\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Tickets: $8 \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				For group and/or single tickets\, contact our School-Time Coordinator at\n607-735-2777 or janices@clemenscenter.org\n			\n				Order Form\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				School-Time Information>\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				View Seating Chart (PDF)\n			\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				A Clemens Center Mary Tripp Marks School-Time Series production presented by Tim Collins\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Experience the haunting power of Edgar Allan Poe’s timeless tales and poems in this innovative performance by award-winning solo performer Tim Collins\, backed by a talented ensemble of actors. Overflowing with the famed writer’s most legendary stories and poems (such as The Raven\, Annabel Lee\, and The Tell-Tale Heart) this darkly compelling performance includes a rich selection of fascinating\, funny\, and moving anecdotes about Poe’s life and work.  \n  \nCurriculum Ties: Literature\, Historical Events\, Social Class\, Inequality \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Dates/times/programs are subject to change.\n			\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				School-Time Information>\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				View Seating Chart (PDF)\n			\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n			\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Ticket prices vary for each performance and are either Reserved or General Admission seating. For patrons with special needs\, please inquire about services when placing your order. \nThe Clemens Center Box Office and ClemensCenter.org are the only OFFICIAL and AUTHORIZED sellers of Clemens Center event tickets. Tickets purchased from other sources may be 1) more expensive 2) invalid and 3) ineligible for assistance. The Clemens Center is not responsible for tickets purchased from other sources.
