SUMMARY:Beetlejuice
DESCRIPTION:BEETLEJUICE\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Tuesday – WednesdayDecember 8 – 9\, 20267:30pm \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Age Recommendation: Recommended for 13+. Contains strong language and mature references. \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Running Time: 2hrs and 30 mins with a 15-min intermission \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n\n\n\n\n Share: \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Pricing\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Processing and facility maintenance fees apply.\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Broadway Series Subscription:\n$349 – $553\n			\n				BUY NOW\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Learn More about our Series Subscription >\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				View Seating Chart (PDF)\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Questions?\nContact our Box Office:\nMonday-Friday\n11:30 am – 5:30 pm\n607-734-8191 or\n800-724-0159\nboxoffice@clemenscenter.org\n\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Visitor Information>\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Learn more about ouronline ticket process > \n			\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				He earned his stripes on Broadway… now the ghost-with-the-most is coming to Elmira.  \nIt’s showtime! Based on Tim Burton’s dearly beloved film\, this hilarious musical tells the story of Lydia Deetz\, a strange and unusual teenager whose whole life changes when she meets a recently deceased couple and a demon with a thing for stripes. With an irreverent book and a score that’s out of this Netherworld\, BEETLEJUICE is “SCREAMINGLY GOOD FUN!” (Variety). And under its uproarious surface (six feet under\, to be exact)\, it’s a remarkably touching show about family\, love\, and making the most of every Day-O! \n			\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				We are very thankful for our organization supporters:\n			\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Dates/times/prices/programs are subject to change.\n			\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				View Seating Chart (PDF)\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Questions?\nContact our Box Office:\nMonday-Friday\n11:30 am – 5:30 pm\n607-734-8191 or\n800-724-0159\nboxoffice@clemenscenter.org\n\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Visitor Information>\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Learn more about ouronline ticket process > \n			\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n			\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Ticket prices vary for each performance and are either Reserved or General Admission seating. For patrons with special needs\, please inquire about services when placing your order. \nThe Clemens Center Box Office and ClemensCenter.org are the only OFFICIAL and AUTHORIZED sellers of Clemens Center event tickets. Tickets purchased from other sources may be 1) more expensive 2) invalid and 3) ineligible for assistance. The Clemens Center is not responsible for tickets purchased from other sources.
