SUMMARY:I Want a Hippopotamus for Christmas
DESCRIPTION:I Want a Hippopotamus for Christmas\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				WednesdayDecember 16\, 202610:00am and 12:30pm \n  \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Runtime: 60 minutes\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Age Recommendation: Grades Pre K – 3 \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n\n\n\n\n Share: \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Pricing\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Tickets: $8 \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				For group and/or single tickets\, contact our School-Time Coordinator at\n607-735-2777 or  janices@clemenscenter.org\n			\n				Order Form\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				School-Time Information>\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				View Seating Chart (PDF)\n			\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				A Clemens Center Mary Tripp Marks School-Time Series production presented by The Barter Players\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				It’s Christmas time at the Ypsilanti Zoo\, and everyone there eagerly anticipates the birth of Bella\, the zoo’s first baby hippo. Seven-year old Lois Jean\, the zookeeper’s daughter\, is especially excited—she’s counting on Bella to reunite her family in time for the holidays. Then the unexpected happens\, and only one person can prevent tragedy. Will Santa arrive in time to save Bella—and Christmas? A heartwarming musical adventure for the whole family! \nCurriculum Ties: Language Arts\, Theatre Arts\, Music \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Dates/times/programs are subject to change.\n			\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				School-Time Information>\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				View Seating Chart (PDF)\n			\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n			\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Ticket prices vary for each performance and are either Reserved or General Admission seating. For patrons with special needs\, please inquire about services when placing your order. \nThe Clemens Center Box Office and ClemensCenter.org are the only OFFICIAL and AUTHORIZED sellers of Clemens Center event tickets. Tickets purchased from other sources may be 1) more expensive 2) invalid and 3) ineligible for assistance. The Clemens Center is not responsible for tickets purchased from other sources.
