SUMMARY:Heroes of the Underground Railroad
DESCRIPTION:Heroes of the Underground Railroad\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				FridayFebruary 5\, 202710:00am and 12:30pm \n  \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Runtime: 60 minutes\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Age Recommendation:Grades 3 – 7 \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n\n\n Share: \n \n\n\n\n\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Pricing\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Tickets: $8 \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				For group and/or single tickets\, contact our School-Time Coordinator at\n607-735-2777 or  janices@clemenscenter.org\n			\n				Order Form\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				School-Time Information>\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				View Seating Chart (PDF)\n			\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				A Clemens Center Mary Tripp Marks School-Time Series production presented by Bright Star Touring Theatre\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				During one of the darkest periods of American History\, thousands of enslaved people undertook a harrowing journey to find freedom. That story comes to life in Heroes of the Underground Railroad. This play highlights several of the heroic stories of the brave men and women who dared to escape slavery\, and the abolitionists who risked everything to aid them along the way.  Your audiences will be amazed at the heroics of Harriet Tubman\, Henry “Box” Brown\, Frederick Douglass\, Levi Coffin\, and John Parker in this incredible show of true American Heroes. \n  \nCurriculum Ties: Reading\, Activism\, School Life \n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Dates/times/programs are subject to change.\n			\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				School-Time Information>\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				View Seating Chart (PDF)\n			\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n			\n			\n				\n				\n			\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				\n				Ticket prices vary for each performance and are either Reserved or General Admission seating. For patrons with special needs\, please inquire about services when placing your order. \nThe Clemens Center Box Office and ClemensCenter.org are the only OFFICIAL and AUTHORIZED sellers of Clemens Center event tickets. Tickets purchased from other sources may be 1) more expensive 2) invalid and 3) ineligible for assistance. The Clemens Center is not responsible for tickets purchased from other sources.
